/ Reference for ChipHelper and documents/_item: every chip and both rows of a
/ Drucksachen list with real records, the call that makes them and where they
/ belong. Not routed in production.
- location = @locations.first
- quarter = @quarters.first
- topic = @topics.first
- district = @districts.first

.kitchensink
  .card.p-4.p-lg-5.mb-5.bg-body-tertiary.rounded-3
    p.text-uppercase.fw-bold.small.text-secondary.mb-2 Kitchensink
    h1.display-6.fw-bold.mb-3 Chips, badges and lists
    .row.g-4
      .col-lg-6
        h2.h6 The shape says what a chip is
        p.small.mb-0
          | A pill is a topic. A rounded rectangle is a place, a Stadtteil or a Bezirk; a place carries a pin, a
            Bezirk its town hall, a Stadtteil nothing.
      .col-lg-6
        h2.h6 The fill says what it does
        p.small.mb-0
          | Outline links somewhere or is an option not chosen. Filled gray is the chosen option. Filled with × is
            a filter in effect, × removes it. Every chip for a thing leads to it. Only the example searches below a
            search field have colour: they are neither a thing nor a filter.
    p.small.text-secondary.mt-3.mb-0
      | Build them with ChipHelper, not with classes by hand. dense: true takes the vertical padding off, for chips
        inside a list row or a card.

  section.mb-5
    h2.h4 Chips
    .table-responsive
      table.table.align-middle
        thead
          tr
            th scope='col' Chip
            th scope='col' Looks like
            th scope='col' Call
            th scope='col' Use for
        tbody
          - if location
            tr
              th scope='row' Ort
              td
                .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-1
                  - @locations.each do |place|
                    = place_chip(place, dense: true)
              td: code place_chip(location, dense: true)
              td.small Places a Drucksache mentions: search results, Stadtteil page, Drucksache, location page.
                At most three in a list row, then "+ n weitere".
          - if quarter
            tr
              th scope='row' Stadtteil
              td
                .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
                  - @quarters.each do |entry|
                    = quarter_chip(entry)
              td: code quarter_chip(quarter)
              td.small "Ihr Stadtteil" on the district page, Nachbarstadtteile, a Drucksache's Stadtteile.
            tr
              th scope='row' Stadtteil, dense
              td
                .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-1
                  - @quarters.each do |entry|
                    = quarter_chip(entry, dense: true)
              td: code quarter_chip(quarter, dense: true)
              td.small Inside a card or a row, such as the streets a search finds.
          - if topic
            tr
              th scope='row' Thema
              td
                .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-1
                  - @topics.each do |entry|
                    = topic_chip(entry, topic_path(topic: entry, district: nil), dense: true)
              td: code topic_chip(topic, url, dense: true)
              td.small A Drucksache's topics, in search results and on the Drucksache. url is the topic page or the
                current list narrowed to the topic.
            tr
              th scope='row' Thema filter
              td
                .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
                  = filter_chip('Alle Themen', '#', selected: true, pill: true)
                  - @topics.each_with_index do |entry, index|
                    = filter_chip(entry.label, '#', selected: false, count: 1200 / (index + 1), pill: true)
              td: code filter_chip(topic.label, url, selected:, count:, pill: true)
              td.small Narrowing a list by topic where no sidebar fits; the list of further topics on topic pages.
          - if district
            tr
              th scope='row' Bezirk filter
              td
                .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
                  = filter_chip('Alle Bezirke', '#', selected: false, count: 4321)
                  - @districts.each_with_index do |entry, index|
                    = filter_chip(entry.name, '#', selected: index.zero?, count: 900 / (index + 1))
              td: code filter_chip(district.name, url, selected:, count:)
              td.small Results by Bezirk on search and topic pages, the Bezirk switch on the district page. The count
                is optional.
            tr
              th scope='row' Bezirk
              td= district_chip(district)
              td: code district_chip(district, url = Bezirk page)
              td.small First among the topics and places of a result from another Bezirk than the one being browsed.
                On the search page url is the search narrowed to the Bezirk. Dense unless dense: false.
          tr
            th scope='row' Filter in effect
            td
              .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
                = filter_token("Thema: #{topic&.label || 'Verkehr'}", '#')
                = filter_token('Auch in Anhängen', '#')
            td: code filter_token(label, remove_url)
            td.small Above a filtered list, one per filter, named with its kind. × removes it.
          tr
            th scope='row' Example search
            td
              .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
                - SearchController::EXAMPLES.first(3).each do |term|
                  = example_chip(term)
            td: code example_chip(term)
            td.small Searches to start from, below a search field and nowhere else.

  section.mb-5
    h2.h4 Status badges
    p.small.text-secondary Plain Bootstrap badges; no helper.
    .table-responsive
      table.table.align-middle
        tbody
          tr
            th scope='row' Beta
            td: span.badge.text-bg-warning Beta
            td: code span.badge.text-bg-warning
            td.small Features built on automatic recognition: places, topics, the map.
          tr
            th scope='row' Inaktiv
            td: span.badge.text-bg-secondary Inaktiv
            td: code span.badge.text-bg-secondary
            td.small Committees and parties no longer active.
          tr
            th scope='row' Count
            td: span.badge.text-bg-secondary 3
            td: code span.badge.text-bg-secondary
            td.small How many are selected inside a closed panel. Not bg-primary: the brand red reads as a warning.

  - if @documents.any?
    - page_district = @documents.first.district
    - sample = @documents.first
    - word = document_title(sample).split.find { |entry| entry.size > 5 } || sample.number
    section.mb-5
      h2.h4 Drucksachen lists
      p.small.text-secondary
        | One row partial, in a .list-group.list-group-flush, title first. No ALLRIS link: the Drucksache's own page has
          it. Load agenda_items with their meetings and committees, and the places with their Bezirk.

      h3.h5.mt-4 Full
      p.small.mb-2
        code render 'documents/item', document:, places:
        span.text-secondary< – here as on a page of #{page_district.name}.
      p.small.text-secondary
        | Lists that are the page's content: search, Stadtteil, topic, location and all Drucksachen. After number and
          kind what became of it at its latest meeting (decided, or still on an agenda), then that meeting. The chips
          name only what the list does not already: the Bezirk when it is not the page's, no topic a topic page is
          about, three places at most.
      .list-group.list-group-flush.border-top.border-bottom
        - @documents.each do |document|
          = render 'documents/item', document:, district: page_district, places: document.locations.uniq(&:name).sort_by(&:name)

      h3.h5.mt-4 Full, as a search result
      p.small.mb-2
        code render 'documents/item', document:, places:, words:, excerpt:, topic_url:, district_url:
      p.small.text-secondary
        | The search words marked in title, number and an excerpt; topic and Bezirk narrow the search instead of
          leaving it.
      .list-group.list-group-flush.border-top.border-bottom
        = render 'documents/item', document: sample, district: page_district, words: [word],
            excerpt: highlight_multi_excerpt(sample.full_text.to_s, word), places: sample.locations.uniq(&:name).sort_by(&:name)

      h3.h5.mt-4 Compact
      p.small.mb-2
        code render 'documents/item', document:, compact: true
      p.small.text-secondary
        | Lists beside the main content: new Drucksachen on the district page, related ones on a Drucksache, the feed
          preview. Title, number, kind and the date of its latest meeting.
      .col-lg-5
        .list-group.list-group-flush.border-top.border-bottom
          - @compact_documents.each do |document|
            = render 'documents/item', document:, compact: true
